WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.200
"Can You Reverse Type 2 Diabetes
with a Whole Food, Plant-Based Diet?"

00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:09.520
The goal of lifestyle treatment
for type 2 diabetes

00:00:09.520 --> 00:00:12.560
is to reverse it,
drive it into remission,

00:00:12.560 --> 00:00:16.160
meaning normal blood sugars
on a normal diet without drugs,

00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:18.560
and exactly that
can be achieved optimally

00:00:18.560 --> 00:00:20.400
with a whole food,
plant-based diet,

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:22.800
as I’ve reviewed before.

00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:24.960
For individuals
who have had type 2 diabetes

00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:26.640
for more than eight years,

00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:29.760
often having faced
multiple complications,

00:00:29.760 --> 00:00:31.440
remission may be
harder to achieve

00:00:31.440 --> 00:00:34.240
because a significant number
of insulin-producing beta cells

00:00:34.240 --> 00:00:37.840
in their pancreas
are already depleted.

00:00:37.840 --> 00:00:39.920
Even though full remission
may not be possible

00:00:39.920 --> 00:00:41.360
for all patients,

00:00:41.360 --> 00:00:43.680
most everyone may still be able
to find their way

00:00:43.680 --> 00:00:46.720
towards better health
and improve blood sugar control

00:00:46.720 --> 00:00:48.800
without adding
more medications

00:00:48.800 --> 00:00:50.720
and could even reduce
the medications

00:00:50.720 --> 00:00:53.760
they are already on.

00:00:53.760 --> 00:00:55.280
You’ve heard
of prescribing meds,

00:00:55.280 --> 00:00:57.680
but what about
deprescribing them?

00:00:57.680 --> 00:01:00.800
Deprescribing medications among
patients with type 2 diabetes

00:01:00.800 --> 00:01:02.240
is actually something
that’s more common

00:01:02.240 --> 00:01:03.760
in lifestyle medicine

00:01:03.760 --> 00:01:06.640
because intensive,
therapeutic lifestyle change

00:01:06.640 --> 00:01:08.800
works pretty effectively

00:01:08.800 --> 00:01:11.040
and can result
in substantial and rapid drops

00:01:11.040 --> 00:01:12.800
in blood glucose.

00:01:12.800 --> 00:01:16.320
In order to avoid blood glucose
dropping too low,

00:01:16.320 --> 00:01:18.400
which results in hypoglycemia,

00:01:18.400 --> 00:01:21.280
medications need to be adjusted.

00:01:21.280 --> 00:01:23.440
And the potential benefits
of deprescribing meds

00:01:23.440 --> 00:01:26.000
in older individuals
is extensive,

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:30.320
including reduced harm from
taking many drugs at one time.

00:01:30.320 --> 00:01:33.280
It not only reduces risk
of adverse drug reactions

00:01:33.280 --> 00:01:35.280
and lowers medication costs,

00:01:35.280 --> 00:01:37.120
but it actually improves
people’s ability

00:01:37.120 --> 00:01:39.840
to take the drugs
they need to be taking

00:01:39.840 --> 00:01:43.040
because they aren’t overwhelmed
with managing so many.

00:01:43.040 --> 00:01:45.840
Deprescribing medications is
individualized to each patient,

00:01:45.840 --> 00:01:48.480
but, generally,
most medical practitioners

00:01:48.480 --> 00:01:49.840
will first target the meds

00:01:49.840 --> 00:01:52.880
most likely to cause
dangerously low blood sugars,

00:01:52.880 --> 00:01:57.360
such as sulfonylurea drugs
like Glucotrol or Micronase,

00:01:57.360 --> 00:01:59.360
and insulin.

00:01:59.360 --> 00:02:01.680
When lifestyle medicine
practitioners were surveyed,

00:02:01.680 --> 00:02:03.920
their perceived negative effects
were minimal,

00:02:03.920 --> 00:02:07.120
with things like "pushback
from insurance companies"

00:02:07.120 --> 00:02:09.600
or patients upset
they hadn’t been told earlier

00:02:09.600 --> 00:02:11.680
about the efficacy
of a plant-based diet

00:02:11.680 --> 00:02:14.560
and that less medication
is possible.

00:02:14.560 --> 00:02:16.640
I’d be angry too!

00:02:16.640 --> 00:02:19.520
The list of perceived positive
effects is full of statements

00:02:19.520 --> 00:02:23.200
like "improved patient morale,"
"empowering to patients,"

00:02:23.200 --> 00:02:26.000
and "improved sense
of well-being and hope."

00:02:26.960 --> 00:02:28.560
Check out this randomized
controlled trial

00:02:28.560 --> 00:02:29.840
of a whole food, plant-based

00:02:29.840 --> 00:02:31.360
intensive
lifestyle intervention

00:02:31.360 --> 00:02:33.680
among people
with type 2 diabetes.

00:02:33.680 --> 00:02:36.720
Successfully improving
blood glucose measures

00:02:36.720 --> 00:02:38.720
while also reducing medications,

00:02:38.720 --> 00:02:41.520
compared to
standard medical care.

00:02:41.520 --> 00:02:43.520
More than half of those
in the plant-based diet

00:02:43.520 --> 00:02:44.640
and exercise group

00:02:44.640 --> 00:02:46.400
reduced their
diabetes medications

00:02:46.400 --> 00:02:49.760
compared with only a fifth
of those on the standard care.

00:02:49.760 --> 00:02:53.040
And this was also true for
their heart disease medications.

00:02:53.040 --> 00:02:54.640
Double win.

00:02:54.640 --> 00:02:56.800
And contrary to
what some may think,

00:02:56.800 --> 00:02:58.480
weight loss
wasn’t necessarily required

00:02:58.480 --> 00:03:00.800
to result in remission.

00:03:00.800 --> 00:03:02.400
Just the plant foods
and exercise

00:03:02.400 --> 00:03:04.240
were so powerful together,

00:03:04.240 --> 00:03:06.480
supporting what we already know:

00:03:06.480 --> 00:03:09.760
food can indeed be medicine.

00:03:09.760 --> 00:03:11.280
What about
those other health concerns

00:03:11.280 --> 00:03:12.880
that come along with diabetes,

00:03:12.880 --> 00:03:15.760
such as increased risk
of cardiovascular disease?

00:03:16.400 --> 00:03:18.160
A systematic review
and meta-analysis

00:03:18.160 --> 00:03:19.680
of randomized controlled trials

00:03:19.680 --> 00:03:21.360
found plant-based
dietary patterns

00:03:21.360 --> 00:03:24.080
result in significantly better
glucose control

00:03:24.080 --> 00:03:26.400
and lower
LDL cholesterol levels,

00:03:26.400 --> 00:03:29.840
one of the big risk factors
for heart attacks.

00:03:29.840 --> 00:03:31.040
People also lost weight

00:03:31.040 --> 00:03:33.040
and decreased
their waist circumference,

00:03:33.040 --> 00:03:36.320
which serves as a sort of proxy
for excess visceral fat,

00:03:36.320 --> 00:03:38.560
a kind of fat that can be
particularly detrimental

00:03:38.560 --> 00:03:39.840
to health.

00:03:39.840 --> 00:03:41.360
Type 2 diabetes
is considered

00:03:41.360 --> 00:03:44.720
one of the most psychologically
demanding chronic conditions.

00:03:44.720 --> 00:03:47.760
Just think about all that people
with diabetes have to manage,

00:03:47.760 --> 00:03:49.600
medications,
doctors’ appointments,

00:03:49.600 --> 00:03:51.040
and regularly stabbing
their finger

00:03:51.040 --> 00:03:52.880
to get blood sugar readings,

00:03:52.880 --> 00:03:54.800
not to mention the fears
of going blind,

00:03:54.800 --> 00:03:56.240
going on dialysis,

00:03:56.240 --> 00:03:59.520
and getting parts
of their lower limbs amputated.

00:03:59.520 --> 00:04:01.280
A systematic review
of the effectiveness

00:04:01.280 --> 00:04:04.160
of plant-based diets
on well-being found that,

00:04:04.160 --> 00:04:05.680
compared to standard care,

00:04:05.680 --> 00:04:08.000
plant-based diets are associated
with significant improvements

00:04:08.000 --> 00:04:11.920
in emotional well-being,
depression, and quality of life,

00:04:11.920 --> 00:04:14.320
along with overall improvements
in health.

00:04:14.320 --> 00:04:17.520
As the incidence and prevalence
of diabetes continues to rise,

00:04:17.520 --> 00:04:19.760
the time is now
for clinicians to recommend

00:04:19.760 --> 00:04:21.840
a low-fat, whole food,
plant-based diet

00:04:21.840 --> 00:04:23.040
to all of their patients,

00:04:23.040 --> 00:04:26.000
but especially those patients
living with and at risk

00:04:26.000 --> 00:04:27.600
for type 2 diabetes.

00:04:27.600 --> 00:04:30.400
Whole food, plant-based diets
can prevent diabetes,

00:04:30.400 --> 00:04:32.800
as well as change
the course of the disease,

00:04:32.800 --> 00:04:35.040
by controlling blood sugar
naturally

00:04:35.040 --> 00:04:38.588
with no known
negative side effects.

